.TH PHONE 1.SH NAMEphone \- talk to a user on another terminal.SH SYNOPSIS\fBphone\fRpath.SH DESCRIPTION\fBphone\fRconnects your terminal to another over the communication path named,\fBphone /t1\fRfor instance: it rings until the other end answers, and then what eachof you types appears on the other's screen.  Control-E leaves.  It needsa second terminal, or a serial line to one.